I walk over to a vegetable stall.
I am making a hot soup today.
I look at the many vegetables on the table.
I point at some large winter carrots.
I need carrots for my soup.
There is a vendor standing behind the table.
"Hello," he says.
"Hello," I reply.
"How much do the carrots cost?" I ask.
"They cost fifteen kroner per kilo," the vendor answers.
Fifteen kroner is a good price.
"I will take one kilo, please," I say.
The vendor weighs the carrots.
He puts them in a paper bag.
He gives me the bag.
I pay the fifteen kroner.
I put the bag down in my large bag.
I look forward to the hot soup.
